            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><table class=\"ips-section\"><thead><tr><th>Title</th><th>Status</th><th>Intent</th><th>Period</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Recovery after chest and abdominal trauma</td><td>active</td><td>plan</td><td>18-Dec 24 - 31-Mar 25</td><td>14-year-old from One Arm Point, five weeks after a bicycle crash with left rib fractures, a traumatic pneumothorax (drained, resolved) and a grade II liver contusion (non-operative). Recovering well; pain mild.\n\nPlan: graded return to activity - walking and swimming now; bike riding from January; no contact sport until cleared at the review in mid-February 2025 (liver). Breathing exercises. Seek care at once with abdominal pain, shoulder-tip pain, dizziness or breathlessness. Review by the visiting doctor in 4 weeks, with the Aboriginal Health Worker; family to be present. Telehealth follow-up with the Perth Children&#39;s Hospital trauma team if needed. He wants to get back to football and fishing, and is interested in marine biology.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
            }
